{
  "area": "subtotal",
  "about": "SUBTOTAL (docs/specs/exsheet-functions ticket 16; ADR-0047, 2026-10-10): admitted while a Sheet cannot hide a row, so 101-111 give what 1-11 give. A cell is nested when its Formula, or for a cell of a Spill Range its Anchor's, calls SUBTOTAL or AGGREGATE anywhere in its text, as the seventeenth Windows run read Excel's answers (SH-68); SUBTOTAL passes over every nested cell. A function number that is not whole is truncated, and a ref that can never be a Reference is refused on entry.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "SUBTOTAL-001",
      "source": "observed",
      "description": "Microsoft's example: SUBTOTAL(9) is the SUM of A2:A5",
      "cells": {"A2": "120", "A3": "10", "A4": "150", "A5": "23", "ZZ1000": "=SUBTOTAL(9,A2:A5)"},
      "check": "ZZ1000",
      "expect": {"value2": 303}
    },
    {
      "id": "SUBTOTAL-002",
      "source": "observed",
      "description": "Microsoft's example: SUBTOTAL(1) is the AVERAGE of A2:A5",
      "cells": {"A2": "120", "A3": "10", "A4": "150", "A5": "23", "ZZ1000": "=SUBTOTAL(1,A2:A5)"},
      "check": "ZZ1000",
      "expect": {"value2": 75.75}
    },
    {
      "id": "SUBTOTAL-003",
      "source": "observed",
      "description": "With no row hidden, 109 gives what 9 gives",
      "cells": {"A2": "120", "A3": "10", "A4": "150", "A5": "23", "ZZ1000": "=SUBTOTAL(109,A2:A5)"},
      "check": "ZZ1000",
      "expect": {"value2": 303}
    },
    {
